\"printf\",\"scanf\"]},{\"name\":\"menu\",\"address\":\"0x17fd\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"puts\"]},{\"name\":\"_abort\",\"address\":\"0x11f5\",\"callers\":[\"init\",\"create_cookie\",\"eat_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"msg\",\"source\":\"rdi (caller-provided string)\"}],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"]}],\"attack_surfaces\":[{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"index (scanf %lld, signed)\",\"operation\":\"WRITE to msg[index] heap buffer with size msg_size[index]-1\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"index is read as signed int64 via %lld and compared with signed jl against cookie_num; negative index reaches msg[] array at addresses below 0x4060 and msg_size[] below 0x4160, allowing attacker-controlled pointer dereference for read() destination and attacker-controlled size from msg_size OOB read\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"index (scanf %lld, signed)\",\"operation\":\"READ msg[index] then printf(%s, *msg[index])\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"index is read as signed int64 via %lld and compared with signed jl against cookie_num; negative index reaches msg[] array below 0x4060, dereferencing attacker-selected pointer for printf %s output (potential info leak)\"},{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"input\":\"random_index (fread urandom % cookie_num)\",\"operation\":\"FREE msg[random_index] then swap-remove\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"index is random (not attacker-controlled), but free is called on msg[random_index] pointer; if msg entries are corrupted via OOB edit, free could target arbitrary pointer; swap-remove also leaves stale pointer in msg[cookie_num-1] position temporarily\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"length (scanf %lld, signed)\",\"operation\":\"ALLOC calloc(length,1) and read(0, buf, length)\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"length is signed int64 compared with signed jle against 0x100; negative length passes check but calloc with negative (large unsigned) may fail; read() with negative length may behave unexpectedly\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is PIE amd64 ELF, dynamically linked, not stripped, source file fortunecookie.c, compiled with GCC 10.2.0 (Debian)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Canary, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY, no CET (IBT/SHSTK)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6, loader /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array at 0x4060 (.bss), 32 elements x 8 bytes = 256 bytes, element type char* (heap pointers)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size array at 0x4160 (.bss), 32 elements x 4 bytes = 128 bytes, element type int32\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"cookie_num at 0x41e8 (.bss), 8 bytes, int64, initialized to 5 by init()\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() pre-creates 5 cookies via strdup with sizes 0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40 at msg[0..4], sets cookie_num=5\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie checks cookie_num<=0x1f (signed jle, max 32 entries) and length<=0x100 (signed jle), allocates calloc(length,1), reads content via read(0,buf,length), stores ptr at msg[cookie_num] and size at msg_size[cookie_num], increments cookie_num\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie selects random_index = fread(urandom,1,1) % cookie_num, prints msg[random_index] via printf(%s), frees msg[random_index], then does swap-remove: msg[random_index]=msg[cookie_num-1], msg_size[random_index]=msg_size[cookie_num-1], cookie_num--\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie reads index via scanf(%lld), checks index < cookie_num using SIGNED jl (jumps if less), reads msg_size[index]-1 bytes into msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie reads index via scanf(%lld), checks index < cookie_num using SIGNED jl, prints *msg[index] via printf(%s) with no length limit\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"scanf format for index is %lld (edit_cookie at 0x21c4) and %llu (read_cookie at 0x21c4 same string reused) — both store into 8-byte stack var; comparison is signed jl in both functions\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg array (0x4060) and msg_size array (0x4160) are adjacent in .bss with 0x100 (256) bytes gap = exactly msg array size; msg_size ends at 0x41e0, urandom at 0x41e0, cookie_num at 0x41e8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is Full RELRO (read-only after relocation), .got at 0x3f58 size 0xa8\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) called in init, setting 60-second timeout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Runtime confirmed: menu displays 5 options, create asks 'How long is the message?' then 'Input your message:', view asks 'Which cookie?[0-N]:', edit asks 'New Message:'\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie both use the same format string at 0x21c4 for scanf; the comparison instruction at 0x1681/0x17aa is 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' where rdx=user_index (sign-extended from 64-bit scanf) and rax=cookie_num\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"Negative index in edit_cookie/read_cookie passes signed jl check (negative < positive cookie_num), allowing OOB access to msg[] and msg_size[] at addresses below 0x4060/0x4160 respectively, reaching .data, .got, .dynamic, .fini_array, .init_array regions\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"msg[-1] at address 0x4058 = last 8 bytes of msg_size array region overlap area; msg[-2] at 0x4050; negative indices reach into .bss below msg (stdout/stdin/stderr at 0x4020-0x4048) and further into .data/.got/.dynamic\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F020\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"With negative index in edit_cookie, read() destination = msg[idx] (OOB pointer from below msg array) and read length = msg_size[idx]-1 (OOB int from below msg_size array), both attacker-influenced via adjacent global layout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Exact runtime heap layout and tcache state after init's 5 strdup allocations and subsequent create/free operations\",\"reason\":\"Requires dynamic heap inspection to determine tcache bin occupancy and chunk addresses\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether negative index OOB can reach useful function pointers or GOT entries for read/write\",\"reason\":\"Full RELRO makes GOT read-only; need to calculate exact negative offset from msg (0x4060) to .init_array (0x3d58) = -0x308 = index -97; .dynamic at 0x3d68 = index -94; these are writable but value semantics need S2 analysis\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether eat_cookie's swap-remove creates a UAF or double-free primitive when combined with OOB corruption\",\"reason\":\"Depends on S2 control flow analysis of allocation/free sequencing and whether msg pointers can be corrupted via OOB edit before eat\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether the %lld vs %llu format string difference between edit and view has exploitable semantic impact on index interpretation\",\"reason\":\"Both use signed jl comparison; edit uses %lld (0x21c4), view uses same string at 0x21c4; need to verify if format strings are truly identical or if view uses %llu at a different offset\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, BuildID 84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, not stripped, source: fortunecookie.c, GCC 10.2.0 (Debian 10.2.0-16)\",\"sections\":\".text 0x1110 AX 0x891 | .rodata 0x2000 A 0x266 | .data 0x4000 WA 0x10 | .bss 0x4020 WA 0x1d0 | .got 0x3f58 WA 0xa8 | .init_array 0x3d58 WA 0x8 | .fini_array 0x3d60 WA 0x8 | .dynamic 0x3d68 WA 0x1f0 | .plt 0x1020 AX 0xe0\",\"symbols\":\"msg 0x4060 OBJ 256 | msg_size 0x4160 OBJ 128 | cookie_num 0x41e8 OBJ 8 | urandom 0x41e0 OBJ 8 | stdin 0x4030 | stdout 0x4020 | stderr 0x4040 | main 0x187f | init 0x1232 | create_cookie 0x1399 | eat_cookie 0x14e1 | edit_cookie 0x1628 | read_cookie 0x1751 | menu 0x17fd | _abort 0x11f5\",\"disassembly\":\"main: scanf(%lld)->switch 1-5 | init: setvbuf x3, alarm(60), fopen(/dev/urandom), strdup x5 -> msg[0..4], cookie_num=5 | create: check cookie_num<=31, scanf(%lld) length<=0x100, calloc(len,1), read(0,buf,len), msg[cookie_num]=ptr, msg_size[cookie_num]=len, cookie_num++ | eat: fread(urandom)%cookie_num -> idx, printf(%s,msg[idx]), free(msg[idx]), msg[idx]=msg[cookie_num-1] swap-remove, cookie_num-- | edit: printf(Which cookie[0-%d]), scanf(%lld) idx, cmp idx<cookie_num (jl signed), read(0,msg[idx],msg_size[idx]-1), newline->NUL | read_cookie: scanf(%lld) idx, cmp idx<cookie_num (jl signed), printf(%s,msg[idx])\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
