"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"Negative index in edit_cookie/read_cookie passes signed jl check (negative < positive cookie_num), allowing OOB access to msg[] and msg_size[] at addresses below 0x4060/0x4160 respectively, reaching .data, .got, .dynamic, .fini_array, .init_array regions\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"msg[-1] at address 0x4058 = last 8 bytes of msg_size array region overlap area; msg[-2] at 0x4050; negative indices reach into .bss below msg (stdout/stdin/stderr at 0x4020-0x4048) and further into .data/.got/.dynamic\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F020\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"With negative index in edit_cookie, read() destination = msg[idx] (OOB pointer from below msg array) and read length = msg_size[idx]-1 (OOB int from below msg_size array), both attacker-influenced via adjacent global layout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Exact runtime heap layout and tcache state after init's 5 strdup allocations and subsequent create/free operations\",\"reason\":\"Requires dynamic heap inspection to determine tcache bin occupancy and chunk addresses\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether negative index OOB can reach useful function pointers or GOT entries for read/write\",\"reason\":\"Full RELRO makes GOT read-only; need to calculate exact negative offset from msg (0x4060) to .init_array (0x3d58) = -0x308 = index -97; .dynamic at 0x3d68 = index -94; these are writable but value semantics need S2 analysis\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether eat_cookie's swap-remove creates a UAF or double-free primitive when combined with OOB corruption\",\"reason\":\"Depends on S2 control flow analysis of allocation/free sequencing and whether msg pointers can be corrupted via OOB edit before eat\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"Whether the %lld vs %llu format string difference between edit and view has exploitable semantic impact on index interpretation\",\"reason\":\"Both use signed jl comparison; edit uses %lld (0x21c4), view uses same string at 0x21c4; need to verify if format strings are truly identical or if view uses %llu at a different offset\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, BuildID 84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, not stripped, source: fortunecookie.c, GCC 10.2.0 (Debian 10.2.0-16)\",\"sections\":\".text 0x1110 AX 0x891 | .rodata 0x2000 A 0x266 | .data 0x4000 WA 0x10 | .bss 0x4020 WA 0x1d0 | .got 0x3f58 WA 0xa8 | .init_array 0x3d58 WA 0x8 | .fini_array 0x3d60 WA 0x8 | .dynamic 0x3d68 WA 0x1f0 | .plt 0x1020 AX 0xe0\",\"symbols\":\"msg 0x4060 OBJ 256 | msg_size 0x4160 OBJ 128 | cookie_num 0x41e8 OBJ 8 | urandom 0x41e0 OBJ 8 | stdin 0x4030 | stdout 0x4020 | stderr 0x4040 | main 0x187f | init 0x1232 | create_cookie 0x1399 | eat_cookie 0x14e1 | edit_cookie 0x1628 | read_cookie 0x1751 | menu 0x17fd | _abort 0x11f5\",\"disassembly\":\"main: scanf(%lld)->switch 1-5 | init: setvbuf x3, alarm(60), fopen(/dev/urandom), strdup x5 -> msg[0..4], cookie_num=5 | create: check cookie_num<=31, scanf(%lld) length<=0x100, calloc(len,1), read(0,buf,len), msg[cookie_num]=ptr, msg_size[cookie_num]=len, cookie_num++ | eat: fread(urandom)%cookie_num -> idx, printf(%s,msg[idx]), free(msg[idx]), msg[idx]=msg[cookie_num-1] swap-remove, cookie_num-- | edit: printf(Which cookie[0-%d]), scanf(%lld) idx, cmp idx<cookie_num (jl signed), read(0,msg[idx],msg_size[idx]-1), newline->NUL | read_cookie: scanf(%lld) idx, cmp idx<cookie_num (jl signed), printf(%s,msg[idx])\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":{\"schema\":\"VulnerabilityReport\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"summary\":{\"total_bugs\":2,\"high_severity\":2,\"medium_severity\":0,\"low_severity\":0},\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"title\":\"OOB_SIGNEDNESS_MISMATCH_IN_EDIT_AND_READ_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Signedness Error\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie read the array index via scanf(%llu) (unsigned long long format at 0x21c4), storing a 64-bit unsigned value into a stack variable. The subsequent bounds check uses a SIGNED comparison: 'cmp rdx, rax; jl' (at 0x1681 in edit_cookie, 0x17aa in read_cookie), where rdx=user_index and rax=cookie_num. When the user inputs a negative number (e.g., -1), glibc scanf(%llu) stores 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (unsigned wraparound of -1). The signed jl instruction interprets this as -1, which is less than cookie_num (5), so the check passes. The code then uses this value as an array index: msg[index] at 0x16d2 (edit) / 0x17ce (read) and msg_size[index] at 0x16b6 (edit). Due to 64-bit wraparound in the 'lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0]' addressing, a stored value of 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF computes msg_base + 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF8 = 0x4058 (mod 2^64), effectively accessing msg[-1]. Larger negative values reach further below the msg array into .bss (stdout/stdin/stderr FILE* pointers at 0x4020-0x4048), .data, .got, .dynamic, .init_array, and .fini_array regions.\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg (0x4060, 32x8-byte pointer array)\",\"msg_size (0x4160, 32x4-byte int array)\",\"stdout (0x4020, FILE*)\",\"stdin (0x4030, FILE*)\",\"stderr (0x4040, FILE*)\",\"urandom (0x41e0, FILE*)\",\"cookie_num (0x41e8, int64)\",\".data section (0x4000-0x4010)\",\".got section (0x3f58-0x4000)\",\".init_array (0x3d58)\",\".fini_array (0x3d60)\",\".dynamic (0x3d68)\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"index via scanf(%llu) with negative numeric input (e.g., -1, -4, -6, -8)\",\"entry_function\":\"edit_cookie / read_cookie\",\"data_flow\":[\"User inputs negative number (e.g., -4) via stdin to scanf(%llu) at 0x1665/0x178e\",\"scanf stores 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFE0 (for -4) as unsigned 64-bit into [rbp-0x10]\",\"mov rdx,[rbp-0x10] loads the value into rdx\",\"mov rax,[cookie_num] loads cookie_num (e.g., 5) into rax\",\"cmp rdx,rax; jl — signed comparison: -4 < 5 → passes check\",\"In edit_cookie: lea rdx,[rax*4+0x0] computes msg_size index; mov eax,[rdx+0x4160] reads OOB msg_size[-4] = *(0x4150) = 0 (uninitialized msg[30] low bytes)\",\"sub eax,0x1 → eax = 0xFFFFFFFF (int32 underflow); movsxd rdx,eax → rdx = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"lea rcx,[rax*8+0x0] computes msg index; mov rax,[rcx+0x4060] reads OOB msg[-4] = *(0x4040) = stderr FILE* pointer\",\"read(0, stderr_FILE_ptr, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) → writes attacker-controlled data to FILE struct on heap\",\"In read_cookie: printf(%s, msg[-8]) = printf(%s, stdout_FILE_ptr) → reads FILE struct content until NUL byte, leaking memory\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"Index should be validated as non-negative AND less than cookie_num before use as array subscript. Both lower bound (>= 0) and upper bound (< cookie_num) checks are required.\",\"actual\":\"Only an upper-bound check exists: 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than). There is no lower-bound check (>= 0). The format specifier %llu stores unsigned values, but the comparison is signed, creating a signedness mismatch.\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing lower-bound check (index >= 0). The signedness mismatch between scanf(%llu) (unsigned storage) and jl (signed comparison) allows negative indices to bypass the upper-bound check.\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"OOB array read via msg[index] and msg_size[index] with negative index; OOB write via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1); OOB read via printf(%s, msg[index])\",\"address\":\"0x1681 (edit bounds check), 0x16b6 (edit msg_size OOB read), 0x16d2 (edit msg OOB read → write target), 0x16de (edit read call); 0x17aa (read bounds check), 0x17ce (read msg OOB read → printf source), 0x17e1 (read printf call)\",\"expression\":\"msg[index] where index < 0 (e.g., msg[-4] = *(0x4040) = stderr FILE*); msg_size[index]-1 where msg_size[index] = 0 → size = -1 (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)\",\"target\":\"For edit_cookie: heap memory at the address stored in the OOB-reached pointer (e.g., FILE struct pointed by stdout/stdin/stderr). For read_cookie: same OOB-reached pointer dereferenced by printf(%s).\",\"size\":\"edit_cookie: msg_size[index]-1 = 0-1 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (effectively unbounded). read_cookie: unbounded (printf %s reads until NUL).\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"In edit_cookie, negative index causes read(0, msg[idx], msg_size[idx]-1) where msg[idx] is an OOB pointer (e.g., stderr FILE* at idx=-4) and msg_size[idx]-1 underflows to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF. This writes attacker-controlled stdin data to the memory region pointed by the OOB pointer, corrupting heap/FILE structures.\"},{\"type\":\"OOB_READ\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"In read_cookie, negative index causes printf(%s, msg[idx]) where msg[idx] is an OOB pointer (e.g., stdout FILE* at idx=-8). This reads and prints memory content at the OOB pointer address until a NUL byte, potentially leaking heap/libc addresses.\"},{\"type\":\"INFO_LEAK\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie with negative index reaching stdout/stdin/stderr FILE* pointers dereferences them via printf(%s), outputting FILE struct contents (which contain heap and libc addresses) to the user.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie with negative index writes to memory pointed by OOB-reached FILE* pointers (stdout/stdin/stderr), corrupting FILE structures and adjacent heap metadata.\"},{\"type\":\"CRASH\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"If the OOB-reached pointer value is invalid or points to unmapped memory, dereferencing it in read() or printf() causes SIGSEGV.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E001\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1665\",\"description\":\"scanf format string at 0x21c4 is '%llu' (unsigned long long), confirmed by .rodata dump: bytes 25 6c 6c 75 00 at offset 0x21c4. edit_cookie loads this format at 0x1665: lea rdi,[rip+0xb58] # 0x21c4.\"},{\"id\":\"E002\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681\",\"description\":\"Bounds check is 'cmp rdx,rax; jl 0x1692' — a SIGNED comparison (jl = jump if less, signed). rdx holds the user-supplied index (from scanf %llu), rax holds cookie_num. No lower-bound (>=0) check exists.\"},{\"id\":\"E003\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b6\",\"description\":\"msg_size OOB read: 'lea rdx,[rax*4+0x0]; lea rax,[rip+0x2aaa] # 0x4160; mov eax,[rdx+rax*1]' — uses the unchecked negative index to read from msg_size array. For idx=-4, accesses *(0x4150) which is uninitialized msg[30] low bytes = 0.\"},{\"id\":\"E004\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b9\",\"description\":\"Size underflow: 'sub eax,0x1' on msg_size[idx]=0 produces eax=0xFFFFFFFF. Then 'movsxd rdx,eax' sign-extends to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, passed as count to read().\"},{\"id\":\"E005\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16d2\",\"description\":\"msg OOB read: 'lea rcx,[rax*8+0x0]; lea rax,[rip+0x298e] # 0x4060; mov rax,[rcx+rax*1]' — uses unchecked negative index to read a pointer from msg array. For idx=-4, reads *(0x4040) = stderr FILE* pointer.\"},{\"id\":\"E006\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"read(0, msg[idx], msg_size[idx]-1) call: rsi=msg[idx] (OOB pointer, e.g., stderr FILE*), rdx=msg_size[idx]-1 (underflowed to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF). Writes attacker data to the FILE struct.\"},{\"id\":\"E007\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x178e\",\"description\":\"read_cookie uses the same scanf format string at 0x21c4 ('%llu') for index input: lea rdi,[rip+0xa2f] # 0x21c4.\"},{\"id\":\"E008\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17aa\",\"description\":\"Same signed comparison: 'cmp rdx,rax; jl 0x17bb' — signed jl with no lower-bound check. Negative index passes.\"},{\"id\":\"E009\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17ce\",\"description\":\"msg OOB read: 'lea rdx,[rax*8+0x0]; lea rax,[rip+0x2892] # 0x4060; mov rax,[rdx+rax*1]' — reads OOB pointer. For idx=-8, reads *(0x4020) = stdout FILE* pointer.\"},{\"id\":\"E010\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17e1\",\"description\":\"printf(%s, msg[idx]) call: rsi=msg[idx] (OOB pointer, e.g., stdout FILE*). printf reads from FILE struct until NUL, leaking memory content.\"},{\"id\":\"E011\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie/read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x4060/0x4160\",\"description\":\"Memory layout analysis: msg at 0x4060, msg_size at 0x4160. Negative indices reach: msg[-4]=*(0x4040)=stderr, msg[-6]=*(0x4030)=stdin, msg[-8]=*(0x4020)=stdout. msg_size[negative] reaches uninitialized msg[5..31] entries (all zero in .bss), causing size underflow to -1.\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm glibc scanf(%llu) accepts negative input and stores 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF for -1\",\"Verify calloc(0,1) returns non-NULL pointer in glibc 2.39\",\"Confirm read() with count=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF writes to heap without immediate EFAULT\",\"Verify printf(%s, stdout_FILE_ptr) leaks addresses before crashing\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-002\",\"title\":\"INTEGER_UNDERFLOW_IN_EDIT_COOKIE_SIZE_CALCULATION\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Integer Underflow\",\"description\":\"In edit_cookie, the read size is computed as msg_size[index] - 1. The msg_size array stores int32 values. When a cookie is created with length=0 (which passes the 'cmp rax,0x100; jle' check at 0x13fc in create_cookie since 0 <= 0x100), msg_size[index] is set to 0. In edit_cookie, 'sub eax,0x1' at 0x16b9 computes 0 - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF (int32 underflow). The subsequent 'movsxd rdx,eax' at 0x16bc sign-extends this to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (64-bit), which is passed as the count argument to read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF). This causes an effectively unbounded write into a small heap buffer (calloc(0,1) allocates a minimum 0x20-byte chunk).\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"create_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg_size array (0x4160)\",\"msg array (0x4060)\",\"heap chunk allocated by calloc(0,1)\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"length=0 via scanf(%lld) in create_cookie; then edit the created cookie\",\"entry_function\":\"create_cookie → edit_cookie\",\"data_flow\":[\"User inputs length=0 to create_cookie via scanf(%lld) at 0x13e1\",\"cmp rax,0x100; jle at 0x13fc: 0 <= 0x100 (signed) → passes check\",\"calloc(0,1) at 0x1416: glibc returns valid minimum-size heap pointer (0x20 chunk)\",\"read(0, buf, 0) at 0x1443: reads 0 bytes, returns 0\",\"msg_size[cookie_num] = 0 (stored as int32 at 0x14a9)\",\"User selects edit_cookie with the index of the length-0 cookie\",\"msg_size[index] = 0 is loaded at 0x16b6\",\"sub eax,0x1 at 0x16b9: eax = 0 - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF (int32 underflow)\",\"movsxd rdx,eax at 0x16bc: rdx = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) at 0x16de: writes unbounded data into small heap buffer\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"The size calculation msg_size[index]-1 should be validated to ensure the result is non-negative before use as a read count. Additionally, length=0 should either be rejected or msg_size should store the actual allocation size rather than the user-requested length.\",\"actual\":\"create_cookie checks length <= 0x100 (signed jle) but does not check length > 0 (no lower bound). edit_cookie computes msg_size[index]-1 without checking if msg_size[index] is 0, causing integer underflow.\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"Missing lower-bound check on length in create_cookie (length must be > 0). Missing underflow check on msg_size[index]-1 in edit_cookie (result must be >= 0).\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"Heap buffer overflow via read() with underflowed size\",\"address\":\"0x16b9 (sub eax,0x1), 0x16bc (movsxd rdx,eax), 0x16de (call read)\",\"expression\":\"read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) where msg_size[index]=0 → count=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\",\"target\":\"Heap memory starting at msg[index] (a small calloc(0,1) allocation, typically 0x20 bytes)\",\"size\":\"0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (effectively unbounded, limited only by stdin input volume)\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read() writes attacker-controlled stdin data into a 0x20-byte heap buffer with an effectively unbounded count (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF), overflowing into adjacent heap chunks and metadata.\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"The heap overflow corrupts adjacent heap chunks, heap metadata (chunk headers), and potentially other allocated objects on the heap.\"},{\"type\":\"CRASH\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"Corrupted heap metadata causes crashes on subsequent heap operations (malloc/free). Writing beyond the heap mapping causes SIGSEGV.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E012\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13f6\",\"description\":\"Length check: 'cmp rax,0x100; jle 0x140a' — signed jle, no lower-bound check. length=0 passes since 0 <= 0x100.\"},{\"id\":\"E013\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1416\",\"description\":\"calloc(length,1) with length=0: glibc calloc(0,1) returns a valid minimum-size heap pointer (non-NULL).\"},{\"id\":\"E014\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x14a9\",\"description\":\"msg_size[cookie_num] = length: 'mov DWORD PTR [rdx+rax*1],ecx' stores 0 as int32 into msg_size array.\"},{\"id\":\"E015\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b6\",\"description\":\"msg_size[index] loaded as int32: 'mov eax,DWORD PTR [rdx+rax*1]' — for the length-0 cookie, eax = 0.\"},{\"id\":\"E016\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b9\",\"description\":\"Integer underflow: 'sub eax,0x1' — 0 - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF (int32 underflow, no overflow/carry check).\"},{\"id\":\"E017\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16bc\",\"description\":\"Sign extension: 'movsxd rdx,eax' — sign-extends 0xFFFFFFFF to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, passed as count to read().\"},{\"id\":\"E018\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF): rsi=valid heap pointer (small chunk), rdx=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF. Effectively unbounded write to heap.\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"Confirm glibc 2.39 calloc(0,1) returns non-NULL pointer\",\"Verify read() with count=0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF does not immediately return error\",\"Confirm the heap overflow corrupts adjacent chunks before any guard page is hit\"]}],\"non_vulnerabilities\":[{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie performs swap-remove: free(msg[random_index]) then immediately overwrites msg[random_index] with msg[cookie_num-1] and decrements cookie_num. The freed pointer is overwritten in the same operation, leaving no window for use-after-free. The old last slot (msg[cookie_num]) becomes inaccessible after decrement. random_index is derived from /dev/urandom, not attacker-controlled.\",\"reason\":\"No independent vulnerability. The swap-remove is safe: freed pointer is immediately overwritten, old last slot goes out of bounds, and index is random (not attacker-controlled). If msg[] entries are corrupted via BUG-001 OOB, eat_cookie could free an arbitrary pointer, but that is a consequence of BUG-001, not an independent bug.\"},{\"function\":\"main\",\"description\":\"main reads menu choice via scanf(%lld) and uses a switch statement (1-5, default loops back). No memory operations.\",\"reason\":\"No memory operations or array accesses with user-controlled indices. Menu choice is only used for switch dispatch.\"},{\"function\":\"init\",\"description\":\"init opens /dev/urandom, creates 5 initial cookies via strdup, sets cookie_num=5. Checks 